rights_decisions [rights_sources_lineage evidence] 2026-09-22T18:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P27.2 append-only rights-resolution log: a licence review that resolves UNDETERMINED-recorded claims is a NEW rights_decision row (source -> resolved rights_record), never an UPDATE; readers resolve effective rights through the latest matching decision (ADR-095)
resolution_materialize [resolution] 2026-09-23T12:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P28.1 materialize entity resolution at scale: nullable input_digest (SIG-RECON-020 reproducibility digest) + partial UNIQUE index so the append-only §28 resolution materializer INSERTs ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING and an idempotent re-run over unchanged inputs is +0 (ADR-099)
relationship_materialize [relationships] 2026-09-23T13:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P28.2 materialize the sharing/access relationship network: nullable input_digest (sha256 over the reconciled edge's reproducible content) + partial UNIQUE index so the append-only §29.3 sharing-edge materializer INSERTs ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING and an idempotent re-run over unchanged claims is +0 (ADR-099 posture / ADR-101 surface)
contradiction_materialize [graph_annotations] 2026-09-23T14:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P28.3 materialize the first-class VISIBLE §31 contradiction object (§29 reconciliation + §28 resolver over the resolved spine): nullable input_digest (sha256 over subject + predicate + contradiction_type + sorted claim-id set + lifecycle status + severity) + partial UNIQUE index so the append-only contradiction materializer INSERTs ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, an idempotent re-run over an unchanged spine is +0, and a resolved-by-later-evidence finding lands as a NEW superseding state row (never an UPDATE/DELETE, §3.1/SIG-RECON-021) (ADR-099 posture)
coverage_materialize [graph_annotations] 2026-09-23T15:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P28.4 materialize honest §32 coverage over the resolved spine (counted quantities with NAMED denominators + records-derived bounds + per-agency reconciliation ratios + negative space, NEVER a total): nullable input_digest (sha256 over the reproducible coverage content) + partial UNIQUE index so the append-only coverage materializer INSERTs ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING and an idempotent re-run over an unchanged spine is +0; additive §32.2/32.3/32.5 metric columns (metric_method/metric_label/numerator/denominator/not_evaluable/named_denominator/metric_value) + a no-total CHECK (a counted-quantity row MUST carry a named, non-reality denominator — SIG-METRIC-009/010; a population total cannot be inserted) (ADR-099 posture)
accountability_link_materialize [inference_schema] 2026-09-23T16:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P28.6 materialize the accountability layer (§11.11-11.18 contract/funding/policy/oversight entities) linked to the RESOLVED deployments/orgs (P28.1) + edges (P28.2) as LABELLED L4 inference in inference.derived_fact — a deployment→vendor→contract→funding→policy→oversight chain, each derived link citing its establishing claims (input_claim_ids, §3.1): nullable input_digest (sha256 over the link's reproducible content) + partial UNIQUE index so the append-only link materializer INSERTs ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING and an idempotent re-run over an unchanged spine is +0; the L4 namespace (SIG-ONTO-002) is the procured≠deployed two-layer guard at the storage layer — a contract/procurement claim yields a derived accountability link, never a deployment observation (ADR-099 posture)
research_task_trigger [graph_annotations] 2026-09-23T17:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P29.2 detector/records-request loop: persist the research queue as durable research_task rows written by the detector run over the Round-6 materialized graph — nullable trigger_kind/trigger_ref so every generated task CITES ITS TRIGGER (the materialized contradiction/coverage/relationship that fired the detector), append-only + idempotent via the existing UNIQUE (task_type, subject_id) (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, +0 re-run); additive/back-compat nullable columns (SIG-STORE-042)
materialize_role [resolution_materialize relationship_materialize contradiction_materialize coverage_materialize accountability_link_materialize research_task_trigger read_surface_grants] 2026-09-24T12:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P30.2 the least-privilege read/materialize role the Round-6 materializers + the P29.2 detector run as on the hosted spine (--role sig_materialize): NOLOGIN NOBYPASSRLS, READ = membership in sig_read_public (tier-0 RLS ceiling binds), WRITE = INSERT only on resolution/relationship/contradiction/coverage_record/research_task/inference.derived_fact + the three resolution FK vocab tables, NO UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE and no write on the claim spine; the deploying schema-owner login is granted membership so it can SET ROLE (operator-authorized LEDGER GATE DECISIONS 2026-09-23, ADR-103)
camera_site_resolution [materialize_role review_queue entity] 2026-09-24T18:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P30.2b geospatial camera-site ENTITY resolution (ADR-105): append-only camera_site_match same_as decision log (tier + match_evidence + establishing claims + disposition auto_write|proposed, input_digest UNIQUE for +0 re-runs) + camera_site_run run record written last as the completion marker (M, N <= M, measured auto-write tiers, eval summary); sig_materialize gains INSERT on both + review_item (proposals), no UPDATE/DELETE
entity_identifier_value_trgm [domain_entities extensions] 2026-09-24T19:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.1 bound GET /v1/search (D-P30.4-2): pg_trgm + a GIN trigram index on entity_identifier.value so the API's unanchored ILIKE (min 3 chars) uses an index instead of a sequential scan; NON-TRANSACTIONAL (CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY, never blocks ingest INSERTs); additive, no table/column/row change (ADR-108)
ingest_run_completion [rights_sources_lineage materialize_role access_control] 2026-09-24T20:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.2 append-only ingest-run completion (D-P30.3-1, ADR-109): ingest_run_completion rows record how each execution finished (ok|partial|quota_reached|failed, DB-clock finished_at, claims inserted, the WORM run-row URI) -- never an UPDATE of ingest_run; one live completion per run (partial UNIQUE run_id) + one backfilled row per WORM gs:// run row (partial UNIQUE backfilled_from, +0 re-run); immutability trigger; sig_materialize gains INSERT only (the WORM backfill)
entity_identity_key [ingest_run_completion domain_entities access_control] 2026-09-24T21:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.3 entity-identity guard (D-P30.4-3, ADR-110): entity_identity_key side table, PRIMARY KEY (scheme, value) = the uniqueness the DB enforces for identity-bearing identifiers; guarded writers claim the key INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING before minting (entity FK DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED, so a losing writer leaves no orphan entity); backfilled from every sig.connector.subject identifier, pointing at the earliest-created entity (DISTINCT ON, so it cannot violate the key over the historical duplicate pairs, which stay and carry recorded same_as/distinct decisions); immutability trigger; sig_ingest SELECT/INSERT only
entity_identifier_scheme_value [entity_identity_key] 2026-09-24T21:30:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.3 btree on entity_identifier (scheme, value) (ADR-110): the identity guard adopts a legacy identifier for an unkeyed value instead of minting a duplicate, and that lookup was a scan (0.7-1.7 s custom plan, 19-169 s generic plan per 10k values on 1M identifiers); NON-TRANSACTIONAL (CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY, never blocks ingest INSERTs); additive, no table/column/row change
ingest_run_capture [entity_identifier_scheme_value ingest_run_completion access_control] 2026-09-25T00:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.4 incremental restarts (D-P30.1-2, ADR-111): append-only per-target capture marks (captured = bytes stored in the capture store; flushed = every claim of the capture committed) keyed to P31.2's per-execution run; a restarted execution of the same logical run (source + cadence window, ingest_run.parameters logical_run) skips flushed targets (still counted as seen) and re-processes captured-but-unflushed ones from the stored capture; immutability trigger; sig_ingest SELECT/INSERT only
partner_org_identity_key [ingest_run_capture entity_identity_key] 2026-09-25T12:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.5 partner-organisation identity (D-P30.2-2, ADR-112): the partner schemes (sig.org.name normalized name; gleif.lei, us.sam.uei, dnb.duns, us.dla.cage, us.cgac.agency_code) join the entity_identity_key guard with the backfill of their existing identifiers in the same change (ADR-110 revisit trigger d) -- earliest entity per (scheme, value), deploy fails if any partner identifier stays unkeyed; keys 0 rows on today's spines; FIPS deliberately unkeyed (a shared place attribute); additive, no table/column/row change
resolution_supersede [materialize_role resolution_materialize] 2026-10-02T12:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.7 resolution supersession (ADR-R9-RESIGHT): re-sighting links move an undated claim's latest-capture date, changing the SIG-RECON-020 input_digest — a changed input inserts a NEW decision and the prior live auto row's sys_period is closed first (§16.4, resolution_no_overlap). close_superseded_resolutions(uuid[],text[],text[]) is SECURITY DEFINER so sig_materialize keeps INSERT-only (no UPDATE on resolution); closes only live decided_by='auto' rows whose digest differs, reports live non-auto pairs as 'blocked' (a human override is never auto-superseded and never crashes the batch); EXECUTE granted to sig_materialize only
review_campaign [camera_site_resolution materialize_role review_queue] 2026-10-02T13:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.10 review campaigns (DEEPEN.6): the seeded stratified review sample's append-only tag — review_campaign (label + purpose + full design: strata/seed/n/universe+drawn counts + tool actor) + review_campaign_item (campaign,item,stratum; PK (campaign_id,item_id) + ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING = idempotent re-draw). Append-only, no UPDATE/DELETE grants; sig_materialize SELECT+INSERT both tables and gains INSERT on review_decision so the authenticated curation decide path can run under the least-privilege role; read roles SELECT.
camera_site_human_decisions [camera_site_resolution review_queue review_campaign] 2026-10-02T19:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P31.11 human review decisions into camera-site clustering (ADR-R9-HUMANER): widen camera_site_match disposition CHECK (+human_accept/human_reject/refused — accept applies as a human same_as edge with decided_by=curator, reject records a hard cannot_link relation, a constraint-violating accept is recorded refused never applied, human_conflict stays proposed) and relation_type CHECK (+cannot_link); sig_materialize gains SELECT on review_decision so the materializer reads the verdicts it already may append; append-only, no UPDATE/DELETE
claim_assertion_bindings [camera_site_human_decisions claim_evidence ingest_run_capture access_control] 2026-10-03T12:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.2 typed assertions + actual-capture bindings (SIG-TRUST-001/002): claim_evidence gains extractor_version/extraction_config_digest/binding_status/bound_at (defaults mark every existing link legacy_synthetic); claim gains assertion_map_id/assertion_map_basis (the named versioned default mapping + explicit basis); claim_qualifier gains value_bool/unit/jurisdiction/valid_from/valid_to/extraction_id/rank + widened uniqueness (the six qualifier families, previously defined-but-unwritten); evidence_capture gains capture_classification with provable-only backfill (synthetic for sig:connector:* artifacts, actual for byte-bearing captures, legacy for the rest); NEW append-only assertion_quarantine (immutability trigger, payload_digest idempotency) for fail-closed rejected assertions — auditable by internal elevated roles, never public-readable; sig_ingest SELECT+INSERT on the two link tables + INSERT on quarantine (ADR-121)
partner_org_scoped_identity_key [claim_assertion_bindings entity_identity_key] 2026-10-10T12:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.3 scoped partner-name identity (SIG-TRUST-004, ADR-122): sig.org.name_scoped (jur:<jurisdiction>|<name> when evidenced, else src:<source>|<name>) joins the entity_identity_key guard so identical names across jurisdictions/sources never auto-union; backfill ships with the scheme (ADR-110 (d)), keys 0 rows on today's spines; legacy sig.org.name keys are NOT re-keyed -- each is repaired by a recorded disposition informed by the partner-name-audit dry-run report, never an in-place rewrite; additive, no table/column/row change
shared_temporal_contract [partner_org_scoped_identity_key camera_site_resolution claim_assertion_bindings] 2026-10-11T00:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.4 shared temporal read contract (SIG-TRUST-005, ADR-123): eligible_occurrence(claim_id, belief) SQL twin of the shared eligible-occurrence contract (role=establishes, bound_at<=belief, retrieved_at DESC with capture_id as non-temporal tie); camera_site_execution append-only per-EXECUTION completion/result refs (latest completed execution governs selection; digest-reusing A->B->A still appends a new completion; execution_id idempotent retry +0; backfilled one per existing run); spine_watermark trigger-maintained materialized freshness table closing D-P31.1-1 (O(facets) read replaces the ~10s per-request six-table count; SECURITY DEFINER statement triggers on INSERT/UPDATE/TRUNCATE over every cached-read relation + every materialization relation; SELECT-only grants)
publication_dispositions [shared_temporal_contract domain_entities] 2026-10-12T00:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.5 one publication/correction eligibility policy (SIG-TRUST-006, ADR-124): append-only publication_disposition registry (allow|withhold|restrict|withdraw on entity|claim|artifact|release_artifact; policy version + authority + public-safe reason category + decided_at + evidence/supersedes linkage; immutability trigger, no UPDATE/DELETE grants) + effective_disposition SQL twin of policy.eligibility.latest_disposition (current access overrides history -- a withhold in R2 denies under an R1 rollback) + spine_watermark facet; public roles get safe-column SELECT only (rationale/decided_by stay elevated), sig_materialize INSERT
human_eval_campaign [publication_dispositions materialize_role review_campaign access_control] 2026-10-16T00:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.9 independent blinded human-evaluation campaigns (SIG-EVAL-001/002, ADR-128): the append-only preregistration (campaign + tamper-evident manifest + persisted denominators), sealed-identifier sample (opaque hev-* ids, partition, estimand, stratum, dependency-group, lineage ids, explicit selection_probability/weight/draw_order), blinded packet surface, reviewer x sample x pass assignments, human attestations, append-only same/different/insufficient_evidence reference labels + separate adjudications, and the authorized unsealing registry. Roles sig_eval_admin (prep + released views only) / sig_eval_reviewer (GUC-scoped RLS: own assignments+packets+labels only, label writes pinned to sig.eval_reviewer) / sig_eval_custodian (read-all + release/adjudication writes, cannot mint labels); RLS ENABLE+FORCE everywhere, immutability triggers, no UPDATE/DELETE grants; sig_materialize and the read/export/ingest roles hold NO eval-table grants -- the *_operational views it may read are empty until an operational-scope release, so sealed labels are unreachable from clustering/model-dev by construction.
disposition_decided_at_authority [publication_dispositions] 2026-09-27T14:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.10a single clock authority for publication_disposition.decided_at (SIG-TRUST-006 defect repair within the ADR-124 family -- no new requirement id): the writer stamped decided_at host-side (datetime.now(UTC)) while the eligibility fragments filter decided_at <= clock_timestamp() on the SERVER clock, so under Docker Desktop VM clock lag a fresh disposition transiently future-dated and vanished from the selector (P32.10's 4 intermittent reds); the change re-asserts/pins the DEFAULT clock_timestamp() the registry was created with and comments the authority contract on the column -- record_disposition now omits decided_at unless a documented replay/migration value is passed; existing committed values untouched
intake_storage [disposition_decided_at_authority access_control] 2026-10-18T00:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.16 durable anonymous correction intake (SIG-FIND-006, ADR-135): the isolated `intake` schema — quarantined payload store (intake.report immutable-identity + expungeable-payload, separate restricted intake.reporter_contact), receipt capability digest table (intake.receipt, sha256 only), append-only restricted audit log (intake.event: received/triaged/assigned/review_requested/disposition_proposed/disposition_approved/closed + housekeeping redacted/expunged; applied/published reserved for the P32.16a bridge and refused by the writer guard for every current role), security-definer redact_report/expunge_report, the coarse intake.report_public projection and its intake.public_state SQL twin of the intake_receiver.toml status map. Roles sig_intake_receiver (INSERT payloads + SELECT projection/digest only) and sig_intake_reviewer (SELECT payloads + INSERT events + maintenance EXECUTE); session-role-checked writer guard (current_setting('role')); NO grants to any existing role — receiver cannot write claim/review_decision/publication_disposition and the spine cannot read intake
intake_application_bridge [intake_storage publication_dispositions entity_identity_key claim_evidence claim_assertion_bindings] 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.16a reviewed-correction application bridge (SIG-FIND-008, ADR-135 follow-up): `intake.application` append-only applied-receipt table — UNIQUE(operation_id) exactly-once barrier, FK approval_seq/proposal_seq into intake.event, outcome CHECK (correct|annotate|suppress|delete) with per-outcome result refs (result_claim_id | disposition_id), no mutable status (the row commits atomically with the canonical write + `applied` event). NEW NOLOGIN role sig_intake_bridge: the only role the re-deployed event_writer_guard admits `applied`/`published` under; narrow canonical grants (INSERT claim, UPDATE (sys_period) claim ONLY — close prior belief per §16.6, claim_evidence re-bind, guarded curator mint via entity/entity_identifier/entity_identity_key, ingest_run, publication_disposition INSERT, validation SELECTs) — no review_decision/capture/payload writes; receiver/reviewer roles gain nothing. `sig.curator.handle` joins entity_identity_key guarded schemes (ADR-110(d)) — approving curator handles resolve to one stable person entity used as asserted_by; scheme backfill ships (keys 0 rows on fresh spines).
recovery_apply [intake_application_bridge] 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P32.22 bounded integrity recovery application (SIG-TRUST-008, ADR-141): `recovery_application` — the append-only applied-receipt/resume marker (UNIQUE(action_digest) exactly-once barrier; one row per executed plan action committing atomically with its canonical write so interruption+restart can never duplicate a repair, and a re-plan over recorded digests proposes +0) — plus NEW NOLOGIN role `sig_recovery` with the sig_intake_bridge-shaped narrow grants (INSERT claim, UPDATE(sys_period)-only prior-belief close, INSERT claim_evidence/disposition/ingest_run/entity-identity, validation SELECTs, sig_read_sealed read-scope; NO capture/blob/extraction writes so missing bytes can never trigger a refetch by privilege)
