audit_login [intake_reporter_outcome recovery_apply] 2026-10-08T14:30:00Z Devin <devin@sig-project.org> # P34.43 least-privilege DB logins (SIG-CONF-013, L3 CP-0, G2 ACT-13; ADR-202): catalog-only — the LOGIN role `sig_audit` (NOBYPASSRLS NOSUPERUSER NOCREATEDB NOCREATEROLE, CONNECTION LIMIT 4, member of sig_read_public's §37 read surface, default_transaction_read_only=on, statement_timeout=60s, SELECT on the NEW-16 ingest_run_capture + entity_identity_key the read role omits) and `sig_recovery_login` (LOGIN CONNECTION LIMIT 2, member of L52's NOLOGIN sig_recovery group — its bounded apply surface is the group's, never duplicated). Passwords are provisioned by the P34.43 leg from Secret Manager only (HG-09); the CREATEs are guarded so the deploy converges a spine the leg ran early on.
